Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "UrbanRainyDrivingWithReducedVisibility" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :StateAnomaly ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3, :risk4 ;
    :hasObstacle :roadCondition1 .

:weather1 a :RainyCondition .

:roadCondition1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Wet road surface with reduced visibility due to rain" .

:risk1 a :WeatherRisk ;
    :description "Reduced visibility due to heavy rain" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .

:risk2 a :RoadConditionRisk ;
    :description "Slippery road surface increasing braking distance" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .

:risk3 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Limited visibility of surrounding actors due to rain" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:risk4 a :RearEndCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Increased risk of rear-end collision due to reduced braking efficiency" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev4 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.85"^^xsd:float .

:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .

:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.70"^^xsd:float .

:sev4 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.80"^^xsd:float .
```

Identified Risks for each risk class:

**Risk 1:**
Description: Reduced visibility due to heavy rain
Severity Score: 0.85

**Risk 2:**
Description: Slippery road surface increasing braking distance
Severity Score: 0.75

**Risk 3:**
Description: Limited visibility of surrounding actors due to rain
Severity Score: 0.70

**Risk 4:**
Description: Increased risk of rear-end collision due to reduced braking efficiency
Severity Score: 0.80

---
The scene was classified as a **StateAnomaly** due to the anomalous state of the environment (rainy conditions) rather than any anomalous behavior of actors or evidence-based anomalies. The primary actors (e.g., the yellow vehicle) were not exhibiting anomalous behavior, but the weather and road conditions posed significant risks.